Render specifics:
- Use Docker for Prometheus (Render's native services don't include it)
- Use a Private Service for Prometheus so it's not public-facing
- Backend API connects to Prometheus via internal DNS: prometheus:9090
- Frontend is a Static Site (Vite build output) or served by your backend
4. Android App Approach
Three options, ranked by effort:
Approach	How	Effort
PWA	Wrap your existing React app in a PWA manifest. Users install from browser.	Lowest
Capacitor/Ionic	Wrap React app in a native shell. Build APK.	Medium
Native Android (Kotlin)	Build separately, call same backend API.	Highest
Recommended: PWA or Capacitor
- Your React dashboard already works on mobile browsers
- Add a manifest.json + service worker → installable as PWA
- For a proper APK, use Capacitor (npx cap init + npx cap add android)
Android app connects to same backend API — no Prometheus in mobile app, just REST/GraphQL calls to your API server on Render.
