6. Key Gotchas
- Render free tier spins down idle services — Prometheus will lose data on cold start. Use paid tier or external Prometheus host.
- CORS: Your backend must set Access-Control-Allow-Origin for your frontend domain.
- Auth: Never expose Prometheus publicly. Always proxy through your backend with JWT/session auth.
- Render env vars: Store PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus:9090 as a service env var.
- Android deep linking: Use universal links or custom URL scheme to open your PWA from native Android.
- WebSocket for live data: For real-time sensor feeds, your backend can use WebSockets to push PromQL subscription results to both web and Android clients.
TL;DR: Prometheus holds metrics → your backend queries it via PromQL HTTP API → frontend/android consume your backend's JSON. Deploy Prometheus as a Docker private service on Render, backend as a web service, frontend as static site. Android via PWA or Capacitor wrapping the same React code.
